From 02a4e845b1c83a733f74b245cfa68ac45d790f79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:01:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik(v2): retain legacy identities and coins in both
 indexes

Carry legacy coin kind through both node bridges, transaction protobufs and confirmed/mempool UTXO queries. Store the creating grammar explicitly beside transaction positions, preserving every u32 file offset. Native Rust projections retain the node structural identity; legacy transactions keep SHA256d identities.

Index legacy transaction bytes directly with explicit legacy input selectors and canonical legacy coin frames. Keep legacy scripts out of V2 authorization roots and preserve legacy native-value spends in the asset index. Account for nine-byte legacy outputs with a derived staging counter bound; keep record and query budgets.

Add focused Rust/native codec, identity, offset, asset and host tests plus a functional legacy-chain-to-v7 bridge check.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
0002-retain-legacy-identities-and-coins.patch: Distinct authored legacy identities/coins indexing purpose, not a fixup.; 0042-t1-rust-msrv-staging-lints.patch: Same-purpose introduced defect; original named owner retained.; 0053-legacy-chronik-protobuf-fixtures.patch: Same-purpose introduced defect; original named owner retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.
